(6440559, 954957, 114969, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your blue ribbon!<br/>I have to say I disagree with all the comments saying it''s the victory of "photography" against "digital art", or whatever people call things. I don''t see the point of opposing type of pictures, processing styles, photographers visions, etc. It''s not a war! ;-)<br/>Editing is a tool, just a tool. It can be indispensable, or close to useless, depending on the creation and what is needed to achieve it. Your idea just worked outstandingly that way, and it also appeared to be the best of the challenge, so you won, that''s basically it :-)<br/>Congratulations again!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-10 12:26:31.</i></td>', 'Congratulations on your blue ribbon!I have to say I disagree with all the comments saying it''s the victory of "photography" against "digital art", or whatever people call things. I don''t see the point of opposing type of pictures, processing styles, photographers visions, etc. It''s not a war! ;-)Editing is a tool, just a tool. It can be indispensable, or close to useless, depending on the creation and what is needed to achieve it. Your idea just worked outstandingly that way, and it also appeared to be the best of the challenge, so you won, that''s basically it :-)Congratulations again!', '2011-06-10 13:25:47.000000', '2011-06-10 13:26:31.000000', 0),
(6440561, 954091, 100831, '<td valign="top">didn''t comment on all my favorites during voting so I''M BACK.... I love the compositon and the fading effect. Happy to see it''s a long exposure - terrific entry!</td>', 'didn''t comment on all my favorites during voting so I''M BACK.... I love the compositon and the fading effect. Happy to see it''s a long exposure - terrific entry!', '2011-06-10 13:27:32.000000', NULL, 0),
