(6440828, 955034, 57775, '<td valign="top">I really like this... in voting, before I even understood the Spleen reference (had to read your description to figure it out) this picture already represented that melancholic, axious feeling that comes with existence.  Beautifully done piece of art.</td>', 'I really like this... in voting, before I even understood the Spleen reference (had to read your description to figure it out) this picture already represented that melancholic, axious feeling that comes with existence.  Beautifully done piece of art.', '2011-06-10 19:08:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6440830, 954957, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> I have to say I disagree with all the comments saying it''s the victory of "photography" against "digital art", or whatever people call things. I don''t see the point of opposing type of pictures, processing styles, photographers visions, etc. It''s not a war! ;-)<br/>Editing is a tool, just a tool. It can be indispensable, or close to useless, depending on the creation and what is needed to achieve it. Your idea just worked outstandingly that way, and it also appeared to be the best of the challenge, so you won, that''s basically it :-)<br/>Congratulations again! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree, Christophe. My point was against people who have claimed that basic photography does not stand a fair chance against advanced digital editing techniques. My point is that it is MUCH more about the idea and the execution, regardless of how you get there. <br/> <br/>Congrats again to both of you!</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: I have to say I disagree with all the comments saying it''s the victory of "photography" against "digital art", or whatever people call things. I don''t see the point of opposing type of pictures, processing styles, photographers visions, etc. It''s not a war! ;-)Editing is a tool, just a tool. It can be indispensable, or close to useless, depending on the creation and what is needed to achieve it. Your idea just worked outstandingly that way, and it also appeared to be the best of the challenge, so you won, that''s basically it :-)Congratulations again!   I agree, Christophe. My point was against people who have claimed that basic photography does not stand a fair chance against advanced digital editing techniques. My point is that it is MUCH more about the idea and the execution, regardless of how you get there.  Congrats again to both of you!', '2011-06-10 19:13:29.000000', NULL, 0),
