(6441130, 953826, 39057, '<td valign="top">LOL...so what?  One layer....the point is that this is NOT an expert edited photo and it won the blue. It goes against everything you posted on your photo thread here and in the forums.<br/> <br/>As far as my DQ image. I took a chance and got permission from Irene and used her water drop as a texture. It was deemed not a texture by SC and got a DQ. I took it like a man and used it to learn. I accept the DQ and it is there for others to learn from.<br/> <br/>Oh...by the way, at the time of the DQ it had a score of 5.24+ ...light years in the DPC scale above your fawn...which I gave a 7 !<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i> I just had to jump in....If I''m not mistaken, the Blue Ribbon went to an image that was done with "Basic Editing" rules!...<br/>.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>The blue ribbon winner is excellent.  The author of that image did use one layer, although he might have scored as well using Basic Ruleset.  Read his image comments.<br/> <br/>Unrelated to the winning images, the DQ''d image in the challenge speaks for itself. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'LOL...so what?  One layer....the point is that this is NOT an expert edited photo and it won the blue. It goes against everything you posted on your photo thread here and in the forums. As far as my DQ image. I took a chance and got permission from Irene and used her water drop as a texture. It was deemed not a texture by SC and got a DQ. I took it like a man and used it to learn. I accept the DQ and it is there for others to learn from. Oh...by the way, at the time of the DQ it had a score of 5.24+ ...light years in the DPC scale above your fawn...which I gave a 7 ! Originally posted by hahn23: Originally posted by kenskid: I just had to jump in....If I''m not mistaken, the Blue Ribbon went to an image that was done with "Basic Editing" rules!.... The blue ribbon winner is excellent.  The author of that image did use one layer, although he might have scored as well using Basic Ruleset.  Read his image comments. Unrelated to the winning images, the DQ''d image in the challenge speaks for itself. ', '2011-06-11 09:23:03.000000', NULL, 0),
